// The Python type check: pyright, the checker inside VS Code's Pylance, so the
// editor shows what blocks a push. Nothing is compiled; the annotations are
// read as written. The gate runs it (daily.py).
//
// "strict" over every script, at zero: every parameter and return annotated
// (pyright has no rule for a missing return - keep it that way by hand) and
// nothing Unknown. JSON read from disk is the data boundary: dex.load/db/meta
// return `Json` (Any), the Python twin of docFromRow in the app; the idioms
// that keep it typed are in .claude/rules/data-pipeline.md.
{
  "include": ["scripts"],
  "pythonVersion": "3.14",
  "typeCheckingMode": "strict"
}
